{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["According to the opinion of R. Abraham Ibn Ezra, <b>like the deeds of the land of Egypt</b> refers to the goat-worship (se'irim) mentioned there. And \"and like the deeds of the land of Canaan\" refers to the forbidden sexual relations, for the Canaanites were wicked and sinful in them, as it says at the end (Leviticus 18:27), \"for all of these abominations the men of the land have done.\" And according to the opinion of our Sages in Torat Kohanim (Acharei Mot 9:3), the Egyptians were also steeped in sexual immorality — in all the forbidden relations, and in males, and in beasts — and this is the truth, for a male cult prostitute (kadesh) existed in the land for males from of old until now, and Scripture testifies about them, \"the Egyptians, your neighbors, large of flesh\" (Ezekiel 16:26), and it says, \"whose flesh is the flesh of asses and whose issue is the issue of horses\" (Ezekiel 23:20), and \"flesh\" (basar) is a euphemism, and likewise \"a flow from his flesh\" (Leviticus 15:2), \"her flow shall be blood in her flesh\" (ibid. verse 19)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The citation 'Torat Kohanim (Acharei Mot 9:3)' follows the standard parashah/paragraph numbering of the Sifra; Ramban's manuscript may vary slightly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:10.056555028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}